From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: orangepi5: drop sd-uhs-sdr104 (SD card reliability)

SDR104 at 150 MHz is the fastest, most signal-marginal UHS-I mode and
is a suspected cause of intermittent SD card corruption on this board.
Drop it; the slot falls back to high-speed (50 MHz, 3.3 V), which has a
large signal-integrity margin. Trades SD throughput for reliability.

NOTE: precautionary, not yet proven to fix the corruption (could not be
reproduced on a known-good card). Validated only that the card drops
SDR104 -> high-speed 50 MHz. Revert if a soak proves SDR104 is innocent.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
index 71d4a6b..ff28e4b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
@@ -751,7 +751,6 @@
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	disable-wp;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_3v3_sd_s0>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vccio_sd_s0>;
 	status = "okay";
